# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages, which serves the built frontend in
# production. Keep these in step with frontend/nginx.conf.template, which
# serves the same files from the container image. connect-src is 'self' here
# because the API is reached through this site's own /api proxy.
#
# Found by the ZAP baseline scan (.github/workflows/zap-baseline.yml):
# - style-src has no 'unsafe-inline': the production build links its CSS from
#   a file and injects no <style> tag (only Vite's dev server does).
# - Pages adds Access-Control-Allow-Origin: * to static files by default; "!"
#   removes it, so no other site's scripts can read these responses.
# - HSTS: browsers already force HTTPS on .dev addresses (preloaded), but the
#   header says so for every client. includeSubDomains covers the preview
#   deployments, which are all HTTPS too.
# - Permissions-Policy switches off device features the app never uses, so
#   injected script could not ask for them either. The clipboard stays allowed:
#   the admin screen copies invite and reset links.
# - Cross-origin isolation: no other site's window may keep a handle on this
#   one (COOP), no other site may embed these files (CORP), and this page loads
#   nothing that has not opted in (COEP). Everything it loads is its own.
/*
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; style-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
